# Keep build context small and prevent host node_modules / build output from
# clobbering the production dependency tree assembled inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# EXCEPTION: super-header-interface's dist/ is a COMMITTED artifact, not build
# output. It is a Vue interface extension whose compiled bundle is checked in,
# and directus/Dockerfile bakes it into the image (Fargate cannot bind-mount
# extensions). Without this negation the extension is silently absent from the
# image — which is exactly the class of failure the Dockerfile's build-time
# guard now catches. The four other extensions are plain JS and unaffected.
!directus/extensions/super-header-interface/dist
!directus/extensions/super-header-interface/dist/**
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.husky
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Tests, specs and docs are not needed in service runtime images.
tests
specs
docs
playwright-report
test-results
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
